# Built APKs & Bundles
#
# ⚠️ READ BEFORE "CLEANING UP": the *current* release APK is deliberately kept in the
# tree via `git add -f`, despite the rule below. Do NOT remove it from tracking.
#
# Reason: the in-app updater's primary download URL is a jsDelivr path of the form
#   https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/{owner}/{repo}@{tag}/{file}.apk
# and jsDelivr's /gh/ endpoint serves REPOSITORY files — it does NOT serve GitHub
# Release assets. So that URL only resolves if the APK is actually present in the tree
# at that tag. This was mistaken for a dirty habit, removed in b601159, and the primary
# update path silently started returning 404 as a result (reverted going forward).
#
# Only the current version should be kept; older ones live on in git history.
*.apk
*.ap_
*.aab

# App level build
app/build/
outputs/
build/
*.log

# Local agent workspace (per-machine state, not shared source)
.workbuddy/
